{"parentUuid":"e0de50ea-1bb6-4582-a4f2-a68b9597c5ac","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>15000000 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c0aa1ecd-bc4b-4eab-bf16-5bcf2d33bf3e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:28:20.804Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>15000000 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL","sessionId":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"misty-brewing-feather"}
{"parentUuid":"c0aa1ecd-bc4b-4eab-bf16-5bcf2d33bf3e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuyaua7pkqPP5Vx7Xuej","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three changes are in. I ran the full demo in Chrome on a separate test server: uploaded all four files, generated, and checked the cards. All 45 tests pass. Nothing is committed or pushed yet; say the word and I'll push.\n\n**1. Generate button moved:** the setup page now runs in order: **01 Product context → 02 Your evidence (optional) → 03 Generate**. Step 3 restates what will be generated (\"BMW 5 Series · United States · 18 months · 12 people · deadline 8/10 · Includes 18 rows of your evidence\"), then the button.\n\n**2. Demo files in `demo-data/`**, one per type, all invented and documented as such in its README. Use them with 5 Series G60 and United States:\n\n| File | Content |\n|---|---|\n| `1-customer-feedback.csv` | 8 comments about the glass roof, wireless charging and seats. Three have an empty feature column, so the preview shows auto-matching. |\n| `2-market-data.csv` | 4 rows: dealer survey, benchmark, order mix, service data |\n| `3-global-trends.csv` | 3 trends, e.g. switchable glass roofs by 2028 |\n| `4-past-decisions.csv` | 2 approved decisions and 1 rejected |\n\nThe files are built around a real weak requirement, so the effect is visible on stage. Tested at weight 8 for all four uploads:\n- **Panorama glass roof:** from **#10 (47) to #3 (60)** in Exterior & Utility.\n- **Seats:** to #1 in Interior & Comfort.\n- **Touch screen:** shows the rejected 2021 decision as a red caution: *\"No points added. Check whether that reason still holds.\"*\n\n**3. Uploads in the reasoning:** cards that use your data get an **\"Includes your data\"** marker. The reasoning opens with a **\"Based on evidence you added\"** section that says what each upload contributed, e.g.\n- \"5 customer comments you added (weight 8/10): +1 point of customer demand\"\n- \"2 market data rows and 2 global trends you added: +4 points of market evidence\"\n- \"Past decision you added (…, approved): '…' +8 points\"\n\n**Rule changes along the way:**\n- **Rejected past decisions no longer add points.** Before, any uploaded past decision added its weight, even a rejection. Now only approved ones count.\n- **Feature matching prefers more matching words.** \"glass roof\" was being matched to the one-word feature \"Roof\" instead of \"Panorama glass roof\".\n- **Heated steering wheel** is now under Interior instead of Exterior.\n\n**Before the demo:**\n- **Restart the server** so it serves the new front end.\n- **Watch the signal label:** with the uploads, the roof's label changes from \"Limited\" to \"Solid customer signal\", because the 5 uploaded comments count as customers (28 instead of 23). The reasoning says 5 of them came from your uploads, but the honest caveat on that card disappears.\n- **To reset after a rehearsal**, use **Remove** in the uploads list on the setup page."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":592,"cache_read_input_tokens":530736,"output_tokens":1018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":592},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1018,"cache_read_input_tokens":530736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":592,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e60fd990-3279-45df-92bc-aae494644e60","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfuyau8pqdmNdhzWCF6uj","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"7cb9c627-f606-44a5-a9e5-0831e0dba498","timestamp":"2026-10-11T06:28:30.374Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL","sessionId":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"misty-brewing-feather"}
