{"parentUuid":"584ffd46-b171-4990-8695-aeca9654efd4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv2gqNcWj1B2RwwUbQh7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both Project Diary dropdowns now use the same branded menu as the Vehicle dropdown: **Storyline** and **Project**. Both are ordinary dropdowns in the same row, so I did the second one too. I clicked through both in Chrome and all 50 tests pass. Hard-refresh to see it (Cmd+Shift+R).\n\n- **Look:** same as the Vehicle dropdown: square corners, a dark top edge on the open menu, and the current choice in BMW blue with a bar on the left. The Project dropdown splits its label the same way, \"BMW 5 Series\" with \"G60 · United States\" in grey.\n- **Fits the row:** I kept the boxed look and 40px height of the date fields and buttons next to them, so the row stays aligned.\n- **Behaviour unchanged:** picking \"Last Quarter\" still fills From/To, and editing a date by hand still switches Storyline to \"Custom dates\". The menu updates to match in both cases.\n\nThe change is two lines in `public/app.js` plus a few style rules in `public/readable.css`. It's not committed yet; say if you want it pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":326,"cache_read_input_tokens":548871,"output_tokens":367,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":326},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":367,"cache_read_input_tokens":548871,"cache_creation_input_tokens":326,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":326,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":nul