{"parentUuid":"a6d06271-b5cb-4d9a-947f-71e344b9079d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14912716 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"436451e9-f2cc-4f75-a70e-71a45e06c666","timestamp":"2026-10-11T08:45:53.082Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14912716 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL","sessionId":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"misty-brewing-feather"}
{"parentUuid":"436451e9-f2cc-4f75-a70e-71a45e06c666","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvA5E62zaWLM8MAaWhL9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The walkthrough is ready at **`walkthrough/index.html`**: one 2.8 MB file that opens in Chrome with no server, no internet and no OpenAI calls. Every screen is a real screenshot of the app. I clicked through all 22 steps at 1440×900 and 1920×1080 with real mouse clicks: no errors, no network requests.\n\n**Flow (follows your \"final final slide audio\" transcript):**\n1. **Intro.**\n2. **Demo 1 (9 steps):**\n   - set the upfront requirements;\n   - upload `1-customer-feedback.csv`, check the preview, add the rows;\n   - generate;\n   - in Interior & Comfort, open the reasoning of **Seating comfort (#2, 60 points, no past decisions)**;\n   - **Move up**, then approve with the reason: *\"seat complaints and defects are a real pain point on long US drives, while the audio settings mostly need clearer controls.\"*\n3. **\"That was the brief. And what every team built.\"** with the four steps of the brief.\n4. **The quote** appears word by word: *\"When I join a project during a handover, I have zero context on what was decided before, or why. I'd love to see the project's past decisions and the reasons behind them.\"* — Former Product Manager, Vodafone (quoted with his consent).\n5. **Demo 2 (8 steps):**\n   - a new PM opens the Project Diary and generates the **Onboarding** storyline (real output, zoomed in);\n   - enters their own constraints (24 months, 8 people, deadline 5/10) and generates again;\n   - Seating comfort now leads, tagged **\"Past decision\"**;\n   - its reasoning zooms into the **Decision Memory** section: the previous PM's reason and **+5 points**. Without those points it would tie for #1 (56 vs 56).\n6. **Close:** \"Vehicle projects run for years. PMs change. Decisions shouldn't get lost.\" with Decision memory, Onboarding and Handover. Last line: \"We don't replace product managers. We give them the memory of everyone who came before.\"\n\n**Interaction:**\n- **Advancing:** click the pulsing blue box (it's labelled with the action, e.g. \"Approve requirement\"), or press → / Space; ← goes back.\n- **Navigation:** the chapter names at the top jump between sections; F toggles full screen.\n- **Animations:** screenshots crossfade, the view zooms into the reasoning, and a cursor glides to each next click.\n\n**App changes this needed (also live in the app now):**\n- **Decision Memory feeds reasoning and ranking.** Approvals and rejections recorded in the app, the team's demo history and uploaded past decisions now appear as a \"Decision Memory\" section. Approved ones add 5 points (uploads add their own weight); rejected ones add no points and are flagged as a caution. Before, your own decisions didn't affect the ranking.\n- **Project Diary opens at today:** it used to start at June 2024, which hid all recent activity.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **Decisions in the repo now count.** `data/decision-events.ndjson` holds the team's test approvals (like \"approval granted\"), and these now give +5 points to those requirements in the live app. Clear it before the pitch if you want clean rankings. I didn't touch it; the walkthrough was captured on a clean copy in `/tmp`.\n- **Rebuilding:** `walkthrough/tools/recapture.sh` regenerates the walkthrough after app changes. It calls OpenAI for the wording and the storyline, about 4 minutes in total. Captions are in `walkthrough/tools/build.mjs`.\n- **Dates in the screenshots:** they show today (11 Oct 2026), and the storyline is the real AI output from this run.\n- **Nothing is committed.** The pitch-deck deletion from earlier is also still uncommitted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":251,"cache_read_input_tokens":644007,"output_tokens":1283,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":251},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1283,"cache_read_input_tokens":644007,"cache_creation_input_tokens":251,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":251,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d956ef64-2a68-469c-a348-dcb78870d99f","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfvA5DChrpyWnJUc5EBMK","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"4adbf5bb-73a5-439b-bab9-9709f3067238","timestamp":"2026-10-11T08:46:06.230Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL","sessionId":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"misty-brewing-feather"}
