{"parentUuid":"f1e32b39-968f-41cd-a088-16045ae28dd1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvEcxgCCscb5i6HXj1Dz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CLs6ZFgPSPTLSm4f4Eb3GP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL\" && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport re\nrows=[l for l in open('walkthrough/SCRIPT.md') if re.match(r'^\\| \\d+ \\|',l)]\nclip={2:4.32,3:6.1,4:3.4,5:2.26,6:8.79,7:4.45,8:5.35,9:4.28,10:3.85,11:10.59,12:3.15,16:2.45,17:3.56,18:2.06,19:5.58,20:6.38,21:2.17,22:9.96,23:3.88,24:2.58}\ntot_words=0;over=[]\nfor l in rows:\n    c=[x.strip() for x in l.strip().strip('|').split('|')]\n    n=int(c[0]);a,b=c[1].split('–');sec=lambda t:int(t.split(':')[0])*60+int(t.split(':')[1])\n    slot=sec(b)-sec(a);say=re.sub(r'\\*\\(.*?\\)\\*','',c[3]);w=len(re.findall(r\"[\\w'’,.-]+\",say));tot_words+=w\n    speak=w/140*60\n    flag='' if speak<=slot+0.5 and clip.get(n,0)<=slot+0.5 else ' <-- tight'\n    print(f\"{n:2} slot {slot:2}s clip {clip.get(n,0):5.1f}s words {w:2} ~{speak:4.1f}s{flag}\")\nprint('total words',tot_words,'≈',round(tot_words/140*60),'s of speech in 180s')\nEOF","description":"Check each step's words and clip fit their time slot"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1556,"cache_read_input_tokens":733734,"output_tokens":5501,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2329},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1556},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5501,"cache_read_input_tokens":733734,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1556,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CLs6ZFgPSPTLSm4f4Eb3GP":{"command":"cd \"/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL\" && python3 -I - <<'EOF'\nimport re\nrows=[l for l in open('walkthrough/SCRIPT.md') if re.match(r'^\\| \\d+ \\|',l)]\nclip={2:4.32,3:6.1,4:3.4,5:2.26,6:8.79,7:4.45,8:5.35,9:4.28,10:3.85,11:10.59,12:3.15,16:2.45,17:3.56,18:2.06,19:5.58,20:6.38,21:2.17,22:9.96,23:3.88,24:2.58}\ntot_words=0;over=[]\nfor l in rows:\n    c=[x.strip() for x in l.strip().strip('|').split('|')]\n    n=int(c[0]);a,b=c[1].split('–');sec=lambda t:int(t.split(':')[0])*60+int(t.split(':')[1])\n    slot=sec(b)-sec(a);say=re.sub(r'\\*\\(.*?\\)\\*','',c[3]);w=len(re.findall(r\"[\\w'’,.-]+\",say));tot_words+=w\n    speak=w/140*60\n    flag='' if speak<=slot+0.5 and clip.get(n,0)<=slot+0.5 else ' <-- tight'\n    print(f\"{n:2} slot {slot:2}s clip {clip.get(n,0):5.1f}s words {w:2} ~{speak:4.1f}s{flag}\")\nprint('total words',tot_words,'≈',round(tot_words/140*60),'s of speech in 180s')\nEOF","description":"Check each step's words and clip fit their time slot"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"685d0acb-0b64-4506-9bf6-3f25e294ed30","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CfvEcx9wCpJnr4KjsPR3D","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b0c3b69-0d94-4ba7-8720-ba74afdf202b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T09:46:23.979Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL","sessionId":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"misty-brewing-feather"}
{"parentUuid":"f1e32b39-968f-41cd-a088-16045ae28dd1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cef163e5-3b54-4b6c-a23b-97ecf22b972b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XCUqpGvH85rNYmVjVkipTh","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL/walkthrough/SCRIPT.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"85788efc-eb36-4977-b78c-fe14d5dcb7dd","timestamp":"2026-10-11T09:46:25.166Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL/walkthrough/SCRIPT.md","content":"# 3-minute pitch script for `walkthrough/index.html`\n\nOne row per step of the walkthrough, in order. **Say** is spoken while the step's clip plays (or while the slide is up). **Click** is the highlighted control that ends the step; where it says **→**, press the arrow key (no hotspot on that step). Times are cumulative and assume a calm pace of about 140 words a minute.\n\nTips: let each clip finish before you click (the blue box appears when it is done). If you fall behind, press → during a clip to jump to its end. The bold words are the ones to land.\n\n---\n\n## Opening\n\n| # | Time | On screen | Say | Click |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 0:00–0:10 | Title: \"From thousands of customer voices to requirements a PM can defend.\" | Every new BMW starts with one question: **what should the next one be?** The answers are buried in thousands of customer voices. Let us show you how a product manager turns them into decisions. | **Start the demo** |\n\n## Demo 1: what the challenge asked for\n\n| # | Time | On screen | Say | Click |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2 | 0:10–0:18 | The cursor fills in the product context | First, the PM sets the frame: **5 Series, United States**, 18 months, a team of 12, and the deadline matters a lot. | **Add evidence** |\n| 3 | 0:18–0:26 | Evidence panel; a customer-feedback CSV is dropped in | Then we add **our own evidence**: customer comments, market data, trends, even past decisions. Here, a file of customer feedback. | **Preview rows** |\n| 4 | 0:26–0:31 | Preview table, features matched | Nothing counts until it is checked. **Every comment is matched to a feature**, and the PM can correct it. | **Add 8 rows** |\n| 5 | 0:31–0:34 | \"Generate the requirements\" | Now, generate. | **Generate requirements** |\n| 6 | 0:34–0:45 | Ranked requirements; the cursor opens Interior & Comfort | In seconds, **4,365 real customer findings** become a ranked list, per area of the car. In Interior & Comfort, **seat comfort is number two**. Why? | **Evidence & reasoning** |\n| 7 | 0:45–0:55 | The reasoning opens and zooms in | No black box. **88 customers** raised it. And this bar shows **exactly what the score is made of**: customer demand, timeline, market evidence, competitor data. | **View cited sources** |\n| 8 | 0:55–1:03 | The sources scroll to Competitors, zoomed | And every number has a source, competitors included: **nine signals** from Mercedes and Audi, each linked to the original. | **→** |\n| 9 | 1:03–1:07 | Back to the reasoning | But the AI only proposes. **The PM decides.** | **Move up** |\n| 10 | 1:07–1:12 | Seat comfort moves to #1 | Seats matter more than audio settings, so seat comfort goes to **number one**. | **Approve** |\n| 11 | 1:12–1:24 | Dictation: the reason appears word by word | And I say why, out loud. **One sentence**, transcribed and saved with the decision. *(let the words finish)* | **Approve requirement** |\n| 12 | 1:24–1:29 | The card shows Approved | Approved, **with its reason**. | **→** |\n\n## The turn\n\n| # | Time | On screen | Say | Click |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 13 | 1:29–1:39 | Slide: \"That was the brief. And what every team built.\" | That was the brief: evidence in, ranked requirements with reasoning, the PM decides. Honestly, **that is what every team built.** So we went back to product managers. | **→** |\n| 14 | 1:39–1:54 | Slide: the quote appears word by word | A former product manager at **Vodafone** told us this. *(pause, let the audience read)* Projects run for years. **PMs change. And the \"why\" gets lost.** | **→** |\n| 15 | 1:54–1:58 | Slide: \"Six months later. A handover.\" | So: **six months later**, a new PM takes over. | **→** |\n\n## Demo 2: the memory\n\n| # | Time | On screen | Say | Click |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 16 | 1:58–2:03 | Project Diary; April activity on the calendar | Day one, the new PM opens the **Project Diary**: every decision on this car, day by day. | **Storyline** |\n| 17 | 2:03–2:07 | Storyline menu | We pick **Onboarding**… | **Onboarding** |\n| 18 | 2:07–2:10 | Date range filled in | …from the first decision until today. | **Generate storyline** |\n| 19 | 2:10–2:18 | The written storyline, zoomed | And the project tells its own story: **what was decided, when, and why**, instead of chasing colleagues for weeks. | **→** |\n| 20 | 2:18–2:26 | The new PM types 24 months, 8 people | The new PM sets **their own constraints**: 24 months, 8 people. | **→** |\n| 21 | 2:26–2:29 | \"Generate the requirements\" | Generate again. **Nothing uploaded.** | **Generate requirements** |\n| 22 | 2:29–2:40 | Seat comfort leads, tagged **Past decision** | Seat comfort leads, and it carries a tag: **past decision**. Let us look inside. | **Evidence & reasoning** |\n| 23 | 2:40–2:46 | Decision Memory block, zoomed | There it is: **approved on 14 April by the previous PM**, with the reason in their own words. | **→** |\n| 24 | 2:46–2:51 | Score bar, zoomed on \"Past decisions\" | And it is not just a note. **Past decisions count in the ranking**, right next to customers and competitors. | **→** |\n\n## Close\n\n| # | Time | On screen | Say | Click |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 25 | 2:51–3:00 | Close: \"Vehicle projects run for years.\" | Vehicle projects run for years. People change. **Decisions shouldn't get lost.** We don't replace product managers. **We give them the memory of everyone who came before.** Thank you. | – |\n\n---\n\n### If a judge asks during Q&A\n\n- **\"Is the data real?\"** The 4,365 findings, 88 customers and 9 competitor signals come from BMW's G60 files and the competitor workbook. The uploaded customer comments are labelled demo data, and the app always shows them as \"Your data\".\n- **\"Did you really speak?\"** The app supports live dictation in the browser; in this recording the speech input is simulated, because it was recorded without a microphone.\n- **\"Why 5 points but 9 signals?\"** Points are the score; signals are the sources behind it. More signals add points up to a cap, so no single source type can dominate.\n- **\"What does a past decision do to the score?\"** An approved decision adds 5 points to that requirement for the next PM; a rejected one adds nothing and is flagged with \"check whether that reason still holds\".\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1e32b39-968f-41cd-a088-16045ae28dd1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL","sessionId":"944dad4c-792b-4da5-b8a1-9392d6587dfe","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"misty-brewing-feather"}
