onths later. A handover.\" | So: **six months later**, a new PM takes over. | **→** |","+| 13 | 1:19–1:27 | Slide: \"That was the brief. And what every team built.\" | That was the brief, and honestly, **that is what every team built.** So we went back to product managers. | **→** |","+| 14 | 1:27–1:40 | Slide: the quote appears word by word | A former product manager at **Vodafone** told us this. *(pause, let the audience read)* Projects run for years. **PMs change. The \"why\" gets lost.** | **→** |","+| 15 | 1:40–1:44 | Slide: \"Six months later. A handover.\" | So: **six months later**, a new PM takes over. | **→** |"," "," ## Demo 2: the memory"," "," | # | Time | On screen | Say | Click |"," |---|---|---|---|---|","-| 16 | 2:08–2:15 | Project Diary; April activity on the calendar | Day one, the new PM opens the **Project Diary**: every decision on this car, day by day. | **Storyline** |","-| 17 | 2:15–2:19 | Storyline menu | We pick **Onboarding**… | **Onboarding** |","-| 18 | 2:19–2:22 | Date range filled in | …from the first decision until today. | **Generate storyline** |","-| 19 | 2:22–2:30 | The written storyline, zoomed | And the project tells its own story: **what was decided, when, and why**, instead of chasing colleagues for weeks. | **→** |","-| 20 | 2:30–2:37 | The new PM types 24 months, 8 people | The new PM sets **their own constraints**: 24 months, 8 people. | **→** |","-| 21 | 2:37–2:40 | \"Generate the requirements\" | Generate again. **Nothing uploaded.** | **Generate requirements** |","-| 22 | 2:40–2:51 | Seat comfort leads, tagged **Past decision** | Seat comfort leads, and it carries a tag: **past decision**. Let us look inside. | **Evidence & reasoning** |","-| 23 | 2:51–2:59 | Decision Memory block, zoomed | There it is: **approved on 14 April by the previous PM**, with the reason in their own words. | **→** |","-| 24 | 2:59–3:07 | Score bar, zoomed on \"Past decisions\" | And it is not just a note. **Past decisions count in the ranking**, right next to customers and competitors. | **→** |","+| 16 | 1:44–1:50 | Project Diary; April activity on the calendar | Day one, the new PM opens the **Project Diary**: every decision, day by day. | **Storyline** |","+| 17 | 1:50–1:54 | Storyline menu | We pick **Onboarding**… | **Onboarding** |","+| 18 | 1:54–1:57 | Date range filled in | …from the first decision until today. | **Generate storyline** |","+| 19 | 1:57–2:03 | The written storyline, zoomed | The project tells its own story: **what was decided, when, and why**. | **→** |","+| 20 | 2:03–2:10 | The new PM types 24 months, 8 people | The new PM sets **their own constraints**: 24 months, 8 people. | **→** |","+| 21 | 2:10–2:13 | \"Generate the requirements\" | Generate again. **Nothing uploaded.** | **Generate requirements** |","+| 22 | 2:13–2:24 | Seat comfort leads, tagged **Past decision** | Seat comfort leads, and it carries a tag: **past decision**. Let us look inside. | **Evidence & reasoning** |","+| 23 | 2:24–2:30 | Decision Memory block, zoomed | There it is: **approved on 14 April by the previous PM**, in their own words. | **→** |","+| 24 | 2:30–2:36 | Score bar, zoomed on \"Past decisions\" | And it **counts in the ranking**, right next to customers and competitors. | **→** |"," "," ## Close"," "," | # | Time | On screen | Say | Click |"," |---|---|---|---|---|","-| 25 | 3:07–3:19 | Close: \"Vehicle projects run for years.\" | Vehicle projects run for years. People change. **Decisions shouldn't get lost.** We don't replace product managers. **We give them the memory of everyone who came before.** Thank you. | – |","+| 25 | 2:36–2:46 | Close: \"Vehicle projects run for years.\" | Projects run for years. People change. **Decisions shouldn't get lost.** We don't replace product managers. **We give them the memory of everyone before them.** | – |"," "," ---"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/abdulrafaymohammed/Documents/Privat/Hackathons/EHL Final/Final-Hack-EHL/walkthrough/SCRIPT.